{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-103991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)}\\,\\text{d}x=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+b\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+6|+C,\n$$\n\nfind the value of $a+b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)} & =\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7=A(x+6)+B(x-1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(-6+6)+B(-6-1) \\\\ 7 & =-7B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(1+6)+B(1-1) \\\\ 7 & =7A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)} & =\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{(x-1)(x+6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+6})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+6|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,b=-1,$ and $a+b=1-1=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103991" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-103991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103991" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|+b\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C,\n$$\n\nfind the value of $a+b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)} & =\\frac{A}{3x+2}+\\frac{B}{2x-3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n13=A(2x-3)+B(3x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(3(\\frac{3}{2})+2) \\\\ 13 & =\\frac{13}{2}B \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(-\\frac{2}{3})-3)+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2) \\\\ 13 & =-\\frac{13}{3}A \\\\ A & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=-\\frac{3}{3x+2}+\\frac{2}{2x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{3}{3x+2}+\\frac{2}{2x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{3}{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{2x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,b=-1,$ and $a+b=1-1=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-49604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x-4=A(x-4)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(4)-4 & =A(4-4)+B(4) \\\\ 4 & =4B \\\\ 1 & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-4 & =A(0-4)+B(0) \\\\ -4 & =-4A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)} & =\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x-4}{x(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103989" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)} & =\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{x+2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x+7=A(x+2)+B(2x+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)+7 & =A((-2)+2)+B(2(-2)+1) \\\\ 3 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-\\frac{1}{2})+7 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+2)+B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\ 6 & =A(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)} & =\\frac{4}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+7}{(2x+1)(x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-103988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-103988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n6x+12=A(x+3)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(-3)+12 & =A(-3+3)+B(-3) \\\\ -6 & =-3B \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)+12 & =A(0+3)+B(0) \\\\ 12 & =3A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)}=\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{2}{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6x+12}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{x}+\\frac{2}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-49903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-347077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{2x+2}{(x-2)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-347077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+2}{(x-2)(x+4)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-2)}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x+2=A(x+4)+B(x-2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-4)+2 & =A(-4+4)+B(-4-2) \\\\ -6 & =-6B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+2 & =A(2+4)+B(2-2) \\\\ 6 & =6A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+2}{(x-2)(x+4)}=\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{1}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+2}{(x-2)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{1}{x+4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+2}{(x-2)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)(x+4)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{2x+2}{(x-2)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)(x+4)|{|}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(40)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\  & =ln\\,(\\frac{40}{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-347077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-347077" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-347077" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{40}{7})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-348975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}-8x+12}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-348975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x+12=(x-2)(x-6).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}-8x+12} & =\\frac{3x+7}{(x-2)(x-6)}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{x-6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n3x+7=A(x-6)+B(x-2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=6,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(6)+7 & =A(6-6)+B(6-2) \\\\ 25 & =4B \\\\ B & =\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2)+7 & =A(2-6)+B(2-2) \\\\ 13 & =-4A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{13}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}-8x+12}=-\\frac{13}{4(x-2)}+\\frac{25}{4(x-6)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}-8x+12}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{13}{4(x-2)}+\\frac{25}{4(x-6)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{25}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}-8x+12}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{13}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{25}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}-8x+12}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-\\frac{13}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+\\frac{25}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-6|]}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{13}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)+\\frac{25}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1))-(-\\frac{13}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+\\frac{25}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-\\frac{25}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-348975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-348975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-348975" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{19}{2}\\ln(3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-349041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{15x-39}{5{x}^{2}-19x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-349041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}-19x-4=(5x+1)(x-4).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15x-39}{5{x}^{2}-19x-4} & =\\frac{15x-39}{(5x+1)(x-4)}=\\frac{A}{5x+1}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n15x-39=A(x-4)+B(5x+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15(4)-39 & =A(4-4)+B(5(4)+1) \\\\ 21 & =21B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15(-\\frac{1}{5})-39 & =A(-\\frac{1}{5}-4)+B(5(-\\frac{1}{5})+1) \\\\ -42 & =-\\frac{21}{5}A \\\\ A & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{15x-39}{5{x}^{2}-19x-4}=\\frac{10}{5x+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{15x-39}{5{x}^{2}-19x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{10}{5x+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{15x-39}{5{x}^{2}-19x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(5x+1)^{2}(x-4)|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{15x-39}{5{x}^{2}-19x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(5x+1)^{2}(x-4)|{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(242)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{242}{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{121}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-349041" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-349041" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-349041" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{121}{2})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{4}^{11}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+16x+3=(5x+1)(x+3).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3} & =\\frac{14}{(5x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n14=A(x+3)+B(5x+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =A(-3+3)+B(5(-3)+1) \\\\ 14 & =-14B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =A(-\\frac{1}{5}+3)+B(5(-\\frac{1}{5})+1) \\\\ 14 & =\\frac{14}{5}A \\\\ A & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}=\\frac{5}{5x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{5}{5x+1}-\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5x+1}{x+3}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{11}\\frac{14}{5{x}^{2}+16x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{5x+1}{x+3}|{|}_{4}^{11} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(28)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{8}{7})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-75828" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{3x+4}{{x}^{2}-16}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-16=(x+4)(x-4).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+4}{{x}^{2}-16} & =\\frac{3x+4}{(x+4)(x-4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+4)}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n3x+4=A(x-4)+B(x+4).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(4)+4 & =A(4-4)+B(4+4) \\\\ 16 & =8B \\\\ B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-4)+4 & =A(-4-4)+B(-4+4) \\\\ -8 & =-8A \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+4}{{x}^{2}-16}=\\frac{1}{(x+4)}+\\frac{2}{(x-4)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+4}{{x}^{2}-16}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{(x+4)}+\\frac{2}{(x-4)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+4}{{x}^{2}-16}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-4)^{2}|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+4)(x-4)^{2}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{3x+4}{{x}^{2}-16}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+4)(x-4)^{2}|{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(24) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{24}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1f4250bdf92c2c10beeab68958ced148fb512341396ca5d2b86210b849b8d1b"} {"question" "q-49761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(168)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(17)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{24})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{32})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{36})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "q-49761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{24})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/state.json" "file_sha256" "a789cf3a3cd2361373fe20c32f5873c9e4fabdf95a2b984c2ba01eccd6f66a96"} {"question" "e-506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int  \\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/example-506.json" "file_sha256" "d2b767b6be16ca1d7fdc22f94e9b39480d3b2ef2cb85eb6aa41754fcfceb578f"} {"question" "e-506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\nx^2+3x-4 = (x-1)(x+4) \\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}+3x-4} & =\\frac{5x}{(x-1)(x+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{A}{(x-1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =A(x+4)+B(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-4) & =A(-4+4)+B(-4-1) \\\\ -20 & =-5B \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, by plugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1) & =A(1+4)+B(1-1) \\\\ 5 & =5A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4}  = \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)} +\\dfrac{4}{(x+4)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}+3x-4}\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-1}+\\frac{4}{x+4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\text{d}x+4\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/example-506.json" "file_sha256" "d2b767b6be16ca1d7fdc22f94e9b39480d3b2ef2cb85eb6aa41754fcfceb578f"} {"question" "e-507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_1^4 \\dfrac{2x+3}{4x^2-1} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/example-507.json" "file_sha256" "787d65b79d0b9c2555a626ba9876320c31f5baaa15c641a7221f48ecebb84e28"} {"question" "e-507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n4x^2-1 = (2x+1)(2x-1) \\,.\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3}{4{x}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{2x+3}{(2x+1)(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{A}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(2x-1)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =A(2x-1)+B(2x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(\\frac{1}{2})+3 & =A(2(\\frac{1}{2})-1)+B(2(\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\ 4 & =2B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-\\frac{1}{2})+3 & =A(2(-\\frac{1}{2})-1)+B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\ 2 & =-2A \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{4x^2-1} = -\\dfrac{1}{(2x+1)} +\\dfrac{2}{(2x-1)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+3}{4{x}^{2}-1}\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{2}{(2x-1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{2x+1}\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{2x-1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|)+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+3}{4{x}^{2}-1}\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{2x-1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{2x+3}{4{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{|\\frac{2x-1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042574/example-507.json" "file_sha256" "787d65b79d0b9c2555a626ba9876320c31f5baaa15c641a7221f48ecebb84e28"}] "usage" {"e-507" [] "q-49761" [] "q-49604" [] "e-506" []} "basis" 1559 "retractions" [[17592186069300 :question/problem "Given that\n\n$∫(13)/((3x + 2)(2x - 3))dx = a\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x - 3 & + b\\ln & 3x + 2\\end{vmatrix}+ C$,\nfind the value of $a + b$."] [17592186069303 :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$∫_{2}^{3}\\frac{3x + 4}{x^{2} - 16}dx$."] [17592186068508 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4} \\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068508 :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\nx^2+3x-4 = (x-1)(x+4) \\,\n$$\n\nSo, the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{5x}{x^{2} + 3x - 4} &= (5x)/((x - 1)(x + 4)) \\\\\n&= (A)/((x - 1)) + (B)/((x + 4))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x &= A(x + 4) + B(x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4$, we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5(-4) &= A(-4 + 4) + B(-4 - 1) \\\\\n- 20 &= -5B \\\\\nB &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, by plugging in $x=1$, we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5(1) &= A(1 + 4) + B(1 - 1) \\\\\n5 &= 5A \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4} = \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)} +\\dfrac{4}{(x+4)}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{5x}{x^{2} + 3x - 4}dx &= ∫(\\frac{1}{x - 1} + \\frac{4}{x + 4})dx \\\\\n&= ∫\\frac{1}{x - 1}dx + 4∫\\frac{1}{x + 4}dx \\\\\n&= \\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x - 1 & + 4\\ln & x + 4\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068510 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_1^4 \\dfrac{2x+3}{4x^2-1} \\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186068510 :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n4x^2-1 = (2x+1)(2x-1) \\,\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1} &= (2x + 3)/((2x + 1)(2x - 1)) \\\\\n&= (A)/((2x + 1)) + (B)/((2x - 1))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3 &= A(2x - 1) + B(2x + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(\\frac{1}{2}) + 3 &= A(2(\\frac{1}{2}) - 1) + B(2(\\frac{1}{2}) + 1) \\\\\n4 &= 2B \\\\\nB &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-\\frac{1}{2}) + 3 &= A(2(-\\frac{1}{2}) - 1) + B(2(-\\frac{1}{2}) + 1) \\\\\n2 &= -2A \\\\\nA &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{4x^2-1} = -\\dfrac{1}{(2x+1)} +\\dfrac{2}{(2x-1)}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1}dx &= ∫(- (1)/((2x + 1)) + (2)/((2x - 1)))dx \\\\\n&= - ∫\\frac{1}{2x + 1}dx + 2∫\\frac{1}{2x - 1}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x + 1 & + 2(\\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid 2x - 1 \\mid) + C \\\\ =-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln & 2x + 1\\end{vmatrix}+ \\ln \\mid 2x - 1 \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1}dx &= -\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x + 1 & + \\ln & 2x - 1 & + C \\\\ = \\ln & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x + 1}} & + \\ln & 2x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\ln \\mid \\frac{2x - 1}{\\sqrt{2x + 1}} \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{4}\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1}dx &= \\ln \\mid \\frac{2x - 1}{\\sqrt{2x + 1}} \\mid _{1}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\ln (\\frac{7}{3}) - \\ln (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\\n&= \\ln (\\frac{7}{3}) + \\ln (\\sqrt{3}) \\\\\n&= \\ln (\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{3})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186067332 17592186067333 17592186067334 17592186067335 17592186067336 17592186067350 17592186067351 17592186067352 17592186067353 17592186067354] "immutable_fields" [[17592186067331 :answer-field/correct] [17592186067331 :answer-field/id] [17592186067331 :answer-field/key] [17592186067331 :answer-field/type] [17592186067349 :answer-field/correct] [17592186067349 :answer-field/id] [17592186067349 :answer-field/key] [17592186067349 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
